            <ArticleTitle>Adherence to follow-up recommendations in asthma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>236-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A cross-sectional study showed that 130 out of 1758 (8%) primary school children without a previous asthma diagnosis had undiagnosed asthma. Thirty-eight per cent of their parents refused to visit a general practitioner for this disorder. Factors associated with the refusal were high maternal education, mild symptoms and absence of airway reversibility.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
